# SYRA (AI Commit Professor)

GitHub-like learning platform: students commit Python code, backend runs static analysis + AI grading.

## Structure

```
Tantr/
└── syra/
    ├── backend/     # FastAPI, Celery, Git service, AI engine
    ├── frontend/    # Next.js pages router, Tailwind, Monaco
    ├── database/
    ├── docker/
    ├── deploy/
    └── scripts/     # run-dev.sh, run-backend.sh, smoke-test.sh
```

## Run locally

```bash
cd syra
./scripts/run-dev.sh
# App: http://localhost:3001  API: http://localhost:8000
```

Backend uses SQLite in dev (`backend/.env`). Git falls back to Dulwich if system `git` is missing. Celery optional — API uses in-process analysis fallback.

## Commit pipeline

Create commit → Git storage → static analysis (pylint/flake8/radon) → AI evaluation → `CommitAnalysis` + `Grade` in DB.

## Frontend gaps to know

- Dashboard links to `/repos/[id]` but repo detail page may be missing — build `pages/repos/[id].tsx` before linking.
- API client lives in `frontend/lib/api.ts`; reuse it instead of ad-hoc fetch.

## Principles

- Minimize scope; match existing patterns in backend/frontend.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, API keys).
- Only create git commits when explicitly asked.
